// Native Sepedi / Northern Sotho (nso) canonical-IPA definition — Bantu (Sotho-Tswana, S32; ~5M, South Africa,
// official). Latin orthography. Sibling of the done Setswana (tn) + Sesotho (st), but a DISTINCT language. NO
// machine referee AT ALL (no wikipron/kaikki/epitran) → ⛔ cannot-verify; authored from standard Sepedi phonology
// (Ziervogel & Mokgokong) as a beyond-referee module, the Setswana pattern. Greedy longest-match scan.
//
// Sepedi's profile among Sotho-Tswana: prominent ⟨š⟩→[ʃ] / ⟨tš⟩→[t͡ʃ], ⟨g⟩→[x] / ⟨kg⟩→[kx], the voiceless lateral
// ⟨hl⟩→[ɬ] and lateral affricate ⟨tl⟩→[t͡ɬ]. Plain voiceless stops taken as EJECTIVE ⟨p t k⟩→[pʼ tʼ kʼ] (the
// Sotho-Tswana pattern, per the Sesotho attestations — UNVERIFIED for Sepedi). No clicks. Vowel height (7-vowel
// /i e ɛ a ɔ o u/) is unwritten → default mid [ɛ ɔ]. Tone (H/L) lexical + unwritten → DEFERRED. ⛔ cannot-verify.
// See docs/investigations/nso_native_bringup_investigation.md.
{
    "language": "nso",
    "name": "Sepedi (Northern Sotho)",
    "script": "Latin",
    "provenance": "Authored from standard Sepedi/Northern Sotho orthography + phonology (Ziervogel & Mokgokong). NO machine referee (no wikipron/kaikki/epitran) → ⛔ cannot-verify; a couple of hand examples only.",

